    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you. Could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S023",
      "patient_response": "Nice to meet you, Dr. Smith. Well, um... I guess what brought me in is I just don't feel like myself anymore. I barely talk to people these days. I just go flat and quiet. And work... even getting started on my cleaning route feels like pushing a loaded cart uphill. \n\nLiterally, sometimes, because they bought these new utility carts for the building last month and the caster wheels on them are just terrible. They’re supposed to glide, but they catch on that thick industrial carpet on the third floor. I told Gary—he’s the night manager—I said, \"Gary, these wheels are useless.\" He’s a good kid, actually. He reminds me of this guy I shared a dorm with when I took a couple semesters of college back in '84. Dave, I think his name was. We used to go to this 24-hour diner after studying that had the absolute best cherry pie. They closed it down a few years ago to build a bank, which is a real shame. Seems like every empty lot turns into a bank or a pharmacy now, you know? \n\nBut, uh... I'm sorry, what was I saying? Right, why I'm here. Yeah, just... everything is a huge effort. I just don't have it in me to say much of anything to anyone lately.",
