    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever felt this way, or experienced a period like this, at any other time in your life before now?",
      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Before now? Well... I mean, this current stretch, it’s been building for about a year and five months. Yeah, right around a year and five months, ever since I had to leave my old apartment and my old neighborhood. \n\nI really loved that neighborhood. I was on the second floor, right above this old hardware store. It was so convenient. If my sink leaked, I just walked downstairs and bought a washer for fifteen cents. The guy who ran it, Sal, he always had the baseball game playing on this dusty little radio. AM radio, you know, with that crackly static sound? It’s actually a really comforting sound. You don't hear much AM radio anymore. Everyone's got those little white pods shoved in their ears now. I see folks on my cleaning route doing it all the time. They don't even look up when I empty their office trash cans, just staring at their computer screens with those things in their ears. It’s rude, honestly. Back in the day, people at least nodded or said hello when you walked into a room. My dad always taught me to look a person in the eye when they enter a room. He was a mechanic, worked on transmissions mostly... \n\nBut, um, what were you asking? Oh, if I felt like this before. I don't really know about before. I just know this whole thing started up after the move.",
