    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Since this started about a year and five months ago, have you noticed any changes in your physical health, or have you been diagnosed with any new medical conditions by a doctor?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Physical health? No, I haven't been to a doctor for anything new. I don't really go to the doctor much anyway, to be honest. Last time I went was... gosh, probably when I pulled a muscle in my back moving a couch. That was years ago, back when I lived in the old place. \n\nIt was this heavy floral couch, the kind with the wooden trim along the bottom that weighs a ton. My buddy Craig helped me move it. Craig's a good guy, he works over at the post office on 4th Street. You know, the one with the really nice brickwork out front? They don't build post offices like that anymore. Now they're just these square concrete blocks, no character at all. It's like everything is just built to be cheap and fast. Same with the mops we get at work. The handles used to be solid wood, you could really get a grip on them. Now they're this hollow aluminum stuff that bends if you lean into a tough stain on the tile. And the mop heads? Don't even get me started on the mop heads. They unravel after two washes. I tried telling the supply guy, but he just shrugged. Nobody cares about quality anymore, it's all just... \n\nWait, what did you ask me? Something about the doctor? Yeah, no, no new medical stuff. Just the same old me, I guess.",
