    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever felt like you were receiving special messages from things around you, or felt that people were watching you or talking about you in ways that others might not understand?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S019",
      "patient_response": "Well... yeah, actually. I do get these thoughts sometimes. Mostly about the new landlord and a couple of the people who live in my new building. I just... I get stuck on this idea that they're keeping tabs on me, you know? Like they're watching me through the hallway cameras and passing messages about me to each other. \n\nPeople tell me those cameras are just for the front door, just for security, but I don't know. The red light on them is always blinking. It reminds me of the blinking light on my old VCR. I held onto that thing for years because I had all these tapes of old boxing matches. Sugar Ray Leonard, Hagler, Hearns... the classics, you know? They don't fight like that anymore. Now it's all about who can talk the most trash on social media before the fight even happens. It's a spectacle, not a sport. My uncle used to box a little in the Navy. He was stationed out in San Diego in the late 60s. He brought me back this really cool model ship once, a destroyer. I kept it on my dresser until I was about twenty, then I think it got lost when I moved out of my parents' house...\n\nBut anyway, what was I saying? Right, the cameras. Yeah, I just can't shake the feeling they're using them to watch me and talk about me behind my back, even if everyone says I'm crazy for thinking it.",
