      "doctor_question": "Do you ever hear sounds, voices, or see things that other people around you do not seem to notice?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Well, yeah, sometimes I do. Mostly when I'm working late. When I'm mopping after hours, I'll hear a man's voice say my name, or tell me I've missed a spot. It sounds clear as day, like he's standing right by the stairwell. But when I look, there's nobody there. It's just me and the mop bucket. \n\nThose yellow mop buckets, you know the ones? The wheels always squeak on the left side. I tried oiling them once with some WD-40 I found in the supply closet, but it didn't do much good. WD-40 isn't really a lubricant anyway, it's a water displacer. My dad taught me that. He was a mechanic for forty years, worked on Fords mostly. He had this old Mustang he was restoring in the garage. Cherry red. He spent every weekend under the hood of that thing. He used to let me hold the flashlight for him, but if I didn't hold it exactly where he wanted, he'd get so frustrated. He had a short temper, my dad. Especially after he lost his hearing in one ear. He said it was from working around the engines all those years without ear protection. Nobody wore ear protection back then. It was just different times... \n\nBut, uh, anyway. The voice. Yeah, I hear that guy by the stairwell, but nobody's ever there.",
